    <!-- Relay syntax help dialog. "Relay" is the user-facing name for what the code still calls
         a "chain" (ChainDefEntity, BlockKind.CHAIN, the chainlang module) — renamed on-screen
         only, see CLAUDE.md. The code fragments (e.g. "(Work, Break)", "repeat(N, step)") are
         chainlang syntax, not prose — identical across languages by design, since the DSL
         keywords themselves are fixed (see RESERVED_WORDS), not translated. -->
    <string name="chain_help_title">Writing a relay</string>
    <string name="chain_help_intro">A relay is a list of steps in parentheses, one per line (or comma-separated — whichever\'s easier):</string>
    <string name="chain_help_example_syntax" translatable="false">(Work, Break)</string>
    <string name="chain_help_step_types">Each step is one of:</string>
    <string name="chain_help_step_duration">• A plain duration: 3, 20m, 2h30m10s</string>
    <string name="chain_help_step_reference">• The name of an existing Timer or Relay, to reuse it</string>
    <string name="chain_help_step_repeat">• repeat(N, step) — repeat a step N times</string>
    <string name="chain_help_step_range">• range(start, stop, step) or arange(...) — a numpy-style count sequence</string>
    <string name="chain_help_example">Example: repeat(4, (Work, Break)) runs Work then Break, four times in a row.</string>
    <string name="chain_help_got_it">Got it</string>

